  "student_passage": "Last Saturday, my brother and I (1) ____ (help) Grandma make lunch. We washed three (2) ____ (tomato) and put them beside the sink. Grandma gave us a small knife and showed us how to keep (3) ____ (we) fingers away from its edge. My brother worked (4) ____ (careful), so I watched him before trying it myself.\n\nAt first, my pieces were large and uneven. My brother said his pieces looked (5) ____ (good) than mine, but Grandma just smiled. It was (6) ____ first time I had prepared vegetables for a whole family. After (7) ____ (cut) the last tomato, I put all the pieces into a bowl. We were both proud (8) ____ our work, even though the kitchen table was wet.\n\nWhile the soup was cooking, Grandma talked about the (9) ____ (important) of cleaning as we worked. She said a cook needed space, not just good food. We washed the bowl and dried the table before lunch. Both my mother (10) ____ my grandmother tried the soup. I thought it tasted especially good because we had made it together.",
