  "filled_passage": "Last Saturday, my brother and I (1) helped (help) Grandma make lunch. We washed three (2) tomatoes (tomato) and put them beside the sink. Grandma gave us a small knife and showed us how to keep (3) our (we) fingers away from its edge. My brother worked (4) carefully (careful), so I watched him before trying it myself.\n\nAt first, my pieces were large and uneven. My brother said his pieces looked (5) better (good) than mine, but Grandma just smiled. It was (6) the first time I had prepared vegetables for a whole family. After (7) cutting (cut) the last tomato, I put all the pieces into a bowl. We were both proud (8) of our work, even though the kitchen table was wet.\n\nWhile the soup was cooking, Grandma talked about the (9) importance (important) of cleaning as we worked. She said a cook needed space, not just good food. We washed the bowl and dried the table before lunch. Both my mother (10) and my grandmother tried the soup. I thought it tasted especially good because we had made it together.",
